<h2>Questions from Plymouth property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can a townhome association invoke appraisal for all its buildings at once?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually the association’s master policy covers the buildings under one claim, and appraisal can address the full loss. The policy wording controls, so we review it first.</p></div></details><details><summary>My insurer says the hail hit my roof in an earlier storm. What now?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Gather records of prior claims, roof age and any inspection reports. Whether damage is new is sometimes decided in appraisal and sometimes treated as coverage, depending on the policy.</p></div></details></div>
